<table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" align="center" bordercolor="">
  <tr>
    <td>
      <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" style="border-collapse: collapse" bordercolor="">
        <tr>
          <td align="center" class="text"><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="1A2B3C" bordercolor="">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Earth, Wind and a whole Heap of Fire...</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text">It's a monster update today. Why? Well - because I can do whatever I bloody well feel like - but also because it was a <B>very good</B> couple of days at Club VM. After all the turmoil, upheaval and general drama at the treehouse, we put (almost) all our differences aside to do what Vis Maior does best. <B>Kick the everloving crap out of every single mob we decide to take on</B> So without further ado, I give you the kill list:<UL><br><LI>Mud Ring in Plane of Earth x2<br><LI>Tantisala Jaggedtooth<br><LI>Vine Ring in Plane of Earth<br><LI>Peregrin Rockskull<br><LI>Mystical Arbitor of Earth<br><LI>General Druav Flamesinger<br><LI>Blazzax the Omnifiend<br><LI>Agnarr the Storm Lord (ok, so not strictly Wind, but close enough)<br><LI>Fennin Ro, the Tyrant of Fire</LI></UL>Wait...what did I just say? <B>Mystical Arbitor of Earth</B>? Why ... that must mean we picked up some Plane of Earth "B" keys. And although there are many derogatory remarks I have stored away about the Plane of Dirt, I shall keep my own counsel for the moment, while I bask in the communal glow of success. For yea, we have met the enemy on his territory and we have emerged victorious. OK, enough of the flowery language. If I make this any more cloying, people are going to start sending me dry-cleaning bills for all the vomit-stained clothes.<br>Anyway - all kinds of interesting toys were dished out.  So, here's material for you to drool over.<br><CENTER><TABLE borderColor=#111111 cellSpacing=0 cellPadding=4 width="50%" border=0><TR><TD align="center" width="50%"><P>Grats Rhand<br>  <IMG src="../lootpics/Shroud_of_the_Stonecrafter.gif" border=0 width="453" height="226"></TD><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Flyingpig<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Bracers_of_Earthen_Energy.gif" border=0 width="455" height="226"></TD></TR><TR><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Gluas<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Stone_Etched_War_Sword.gif" border=0 width="455" height="226"></TD><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Razzari<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Clay_Bracers_of_the_Golem.gif" border=0 width="453" height="226"></TD></TR><TR><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Reiny<br><IMG src="../lootpics/War_Drums_of_the_Rathe.gif" border=0 width="456" height="227"></TD><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Xelera<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Earring_of_Living_Earth.gif" border=0 width="455" height="227"></TD></TR><TR><br><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Larsen<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Primal_Mask_of_the_Earthcrafter.gif" border=0 width="456" height="225"></TD><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Tzebastian<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Ornate_Greatblade.gif" border=0 width="454" height="226"></TD></TR><TR><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Lokkin & Melodico<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Stormriders_Gauntlets.gif" border=0 width="454" height="225"></TD><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Reznorr<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Fire_Marked_Rune.gif" border=0 width="454" height="225"></TD></TR><TR><TD align=middle width="50%"><p>Grats Philthyphil<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Blaring_Horn_of_Fire.gif" border=0 width="452" height="220"></TD><br><TD align=middle width="50%"><P>Grats Viciado & Sscylla<br><IMG src="../lootpics/Immaculate_Vest_of_the_Fire_Tyrant.gif" border=0 width="456" height="226"></TD></TR></TABLE></center><br>There were also other goodies dished out:<ul><li>Elemental Silk Pants Pattern - Grats Trinitii</li><li>Elemental Plate Boots Mold - Grats Genalen</li><li>Elemental Chain Bracer Pattern - Grats Ultu</li></ul>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Thursday, July 24, 2003 at 14:59 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="1A2B3C" bordercolor="">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">We didn't start the Fire...we just put it out.</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text">Remember how you always heard that you were playing with fire?  The common interpretation of that saying is that you're taking risks.  Well....welcome to a whole new world.  Cleaning house in the Plane of Fire is about as exciting as getting out of bed.  That having been said, there's always the prospect of ending the night with this sort of image:<br><br><p align="Center"><img src="../images/Fennin_Ro_Dead.gif" border="0"></p><br>I mean honestly - I don't even think a mother could love this face.  Still, <b>Fennin Ro</b> occasionally gives out some decent gear.  Sadly, this was not one of his better nights.  As a consolation prize, we hammered down <b>Jaxoliz Dawneyes</b> and <b>Criare Sunmane</b> just because they happened to be in our way (not really, but they were up, so why not kill them?)  And now the portion for the materialistic among you...<br><div><br><center><table border="0" cellpadding="4" style="border-collapse: collapse" bordercolor="#111111" width="50%" id="AutoNumber1" cellspacing="0"><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><p>Grats Ayend<br><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Blaring_Horn_of_Fire.gif"></td><td width="50%" align="center"><p>Grats Xelera<br><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Fire_Crested_Rune.gif"></td></tr><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><p>Grats Shaekee & Buffmeister<br><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Gleaming_Mesh_Girdle.gif"></td><td width="50%" align="center"><p>Grats Talonz<br><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Shimmering_Sleeves_of_Flame.gif"></td></tr><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><p>Grats Shilude<br><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Shining_Crimson_Shawl.gif"></td></tr></table></div></center><p>Another boring quotes day, well, simply put we were too busy killing things to talk.&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Thursday, July 17, 2003 at 04:38 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="1A2B3C" bordercolor="">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">JUDGEMENT DAY</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><p><b>FOUR GODS, SIX HOURS</b>.  That's the tale of the tape from last night.  We rampaged through the Planes last night in an orgy of madness and mayhem.  Mobs were up all over the place last night, and we took the opportunity to blast through as many as we could find, despite the fact that we rarely had 60 people on-line at any given time.  <ul><li><b>Solusek Ro</b> - Yeah, about as challenging as getting out of bed.</li><li><b>Rallos Zek the Warlord</b> - Like he had a chance.  He lasted about three minutes.</li><li><b>Terris Thule</b> - If she had a mouth her last words would have been, "What the F...?".</li><li><b>Lord Mithaniel Marr</b> - The only thing the Randy Savage lookalike is Lord of now is the Dirt Nap.</li></ul></p><br>Unfortunately Rallos Zek didn't give up Blade of War #4, but oh well.  Several nice loot items to dish out:<br><div><br><center><table border="0" cellpadding="4" style="border-collapse: collapse" bordercolor="#111111" width="50%" id="AutoNumber1" cellspacing="0"><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Orb_of_the_Sun.gif" width="454" height="224"><p>Grats Dojamun</td><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Gold_Runed_Mithril_Knife.gif" width="456" height="225"><p>Grats Citto</td></tr><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Grimfaced_Visor.gif" width="456" height="224"><p>Grats Selaen</td><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Boots_of_the_Warmaster.gif" width="455" height="223"><p>Grats Darmond</td></tr><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Carved_Bone_Ring.gif" width="451" height="224"><p>Grats Shaekee</td><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Sable_Lined_Mantle.gif" width="454" height="225"><p>Grats Kathley</td>   </tr></table></div></center><p>No amazing quotes to post today because, well, simply put we were too busy killing things to talk.<br><br>Some interesting news on the World News Front though.  The United States Navy commissioned the first ever carrier to be named after a living president.  That's right, the <i>USS Ronald Reagan</i> was commissioned at Norfolk on Saturday.  Just when all the psychos in the world thought they were finally seeing the back of President Reagan ...<br><p align="center"><img border="0" src="../images/USS_Ronald_Reagan.gif"></p>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Sunday, July 13, 2003 at 04:16 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="1A2B3C" bordercolor="">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Plane of Boredom and Frustration</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><p>The Vis Maior War Machine took the left turn at Albuquerque that Bugs Bunny kept passing up and wound up in Xegonyville.  No, we didn't go smack the old wench down, we subjected ourselves to a night of masochism in what I consider the one of the most boring zones in EQ.  But hey, that's just me.  Xegony keys were the order of the day - and oh was this raid a rollercoaster.<br>I'm sure I'm not the first person to wish excruciating death and dismemberment upon the Sony programmers for the insane nature of some of the events.  After all, who wouldn't find it highly exhilarating to have 6 1/2 hours of work wasted by a mob whose encounter is so unforgiving that one resisted slow or a CH that lands half a second too late means failure.  Yep, thanks a lot Sony - send some of your Game Designers and Programmers my way - I have a .45 and a shovel, trust me - <b>NO-ONE</b> will miss them...</p><br>Anyway, the night wasn't a total loss, we did pick up some key parts, several items for Gate Neck #3 and several people got some nifty new gear: <center><br><table border="0" cellpadding="4" style="border-collapse: collapse" bordercolor="#111111" width="50%" id="AutoNumber1" cellspacing="0"><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Band_of_Fortitude.gif" width="454" height="224"><p>Grats Darmond</td><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Ensorcelled_Metalcloth_Cape.gif" width="456" height="225"><p>Grats Citto</td></tr><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Air_Fetish.gif" width="456" height="224"><p>Grats Xelera</td><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Sparkling_Shortsword.gif" width="455" height="223"><p>Grats Melodico</td></tr><tr><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Tethered_Air_Cape.gif" width="451" height="224"><p>Grats Kalakar</td><td width="50%" align="center"><img border="0" src="../lootpics/Scintillating_Feather_Mask.gif" width="454" height="225"><p>Grats Dojamun</td>   </tr></table></center></div><p>And of course, as befits a group of people who live on caffeine, pizza, high-speed connectivity and the ability to tap several keys in sequence for hours at a stretch, we have our usual <b>WTF WAS THAT?</b> section....</p><p>Citto seemed to be getting into all sorts of trouble:</p><p><img border="0" src="../screenshots/Saldaria_Citto1.gif" width="454" height="24"></p><p><img border="0" src="../screenshots/Alleusion_Citto1.gif" width="446" height="12"></p><p>Nikochan presented us with an interesting (albeit politically incorrect) sporting quandary....or something:</p><p><img border="0" src="../screenshots/Nikochan_Racing.gif" width="445" height="14"></p><p>And then there was Xelera's latest dream.  This one is definitely a candidate for the Freud Hall of Bizarro Dream Fame.</p><p><img border="0" src="../screenshots/Xelera_Dream.gif" width="458" height="49"></p>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Saturday, July 12, 2003 at 05:31 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="1A2B3C" bordercolor="">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Thank Heavens for Patch Days</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><P>Patch Days.  We love them.  Forget about the fact that pathing may be totally screwed up, forget that lag on patch days absolutely sucks, and forget that some class has usually taken a stealth nerf on the chin.  Patch Day means a smorgasbord of killing opportunities.  First up on our hit list?  That's right <A href="http://eqbeastiary.allakhazam.com/search.shtml?id=10359" target=_blank>Rallos Zek, the Warlord</A>.  Now, given the fact that it's been a hell of a long time since we smacked down old ugly, we were understandably a bit rusty.  What a surprise - we won.  So now, I know that there are people out there who are absolutely dying to know if a certain item dropped...the answer is...<STRONG>Yes</STRONG>.  Congratulations Vis Maior on Blade of War #3.  So far we haven't seen very much wrong with the Rallos Zek itemization, thank you very much.<br><CENTER><TABLE><TR><TD width="100%"><IMG src="http://ww.vismaiorguild.org/lootpics/Blade_of_War.gif"></TD></TR><TR><TD width="100%"><P align=center>Grats Flyingpig</P><P>Since this was our THIRD Blade of War, we felt some Charity was in order</P><P align=center><IMG src="http://ww.vismaiorguild.org/screenshots/FlyingPig_Cleric.gif"></P><P align=center></P></TD></TR><br><TR><BR><TD width="100%"><IMG src="http://ww.vismaiorguild.org/lootpics/Grimfaced_Visor.gif"></FONT></TD></TR><TR><TD width="100%"><br><P align=center>Grats Rasthik</P></TD></TR></TABLE></CENTER>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Friday, July 11, 2003 at 04:07 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="1A2B3C" bordercolor="">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Happy 4th of July</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><p align="center"><br><img border="0" src="../images/ccdhap4th.jpg"></p><br><p align="left">A quick visit to the Plane of Fire last night for some armor upgrades.&nbsp; As usual, we came, we saw, we won, we left.&nbsp; Pyronis, Quavonis &amp; Magmaton fell in quick succession - providing the following new toys:</p><br><ul><li>Elemental Chain Boots Pattern - Feelmore</li><br>  <li>Elemental Leather Boots Pattern - Hechicera</li><br>  <li>Elemental Plate Vambraces Mold - Rasttan </li><br>  <li>Elemental Chain Sleeves Pattern - Gluas</li><br>  <li>Elemental Plate Gauntlets Mold - Grimblades &amp; Sorchaa</li><br></ul><br>Here's a tip for today: <b>DON'T PLAY EVERQUEST</b>  Go spend time with family, friends & do RL stuff.&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                  <tr> 
                <td align="right" class="smItalic">Posted by <a href="mailto:" class="mail" style="font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;">Tovarich</a> on Friday, July 04, 2003 at 05:29 </td>
             	       </tr>
                      </table>
                      </td>
                    </tr>
                  </table>
                </td>
              </tr>
            </table>
            
            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="1A2B3C" bordercolor="">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">VM goes Old School</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><P>Tuesday night was retro-night at Club VM. This was also billed as "A night in Luclin with friends." Now, I'll be brutally honest, I basically skipped the entire Luclin expansin playing Dark Age of Camelot, which meant that Tuesday night I got my <A href="http://eqbeastiary.allakhazam.com/search.shtml?id=7898" target=_blank>Emperor Ssraeshza</A> cherry popped. I'm sure that the Emperor fight was probably a whole lot more exciting before the launch of Planes of Power and the advent of 5 new levels and ungodly amounts of AA points. I'm sure that a 3 Cleric, 1 Druid CH team wouldn't have cut it pre-PoP either. And I'm pretty sure that a flawless kill given that sort of healing power would have been virtually impossible. I'm equally sure that the loot probably wouldn't have been as crappy as it was last night.</P>
<CENTER>
