            <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="2" cellpadding="2" bgcolor="1A2B3C" bordercolor="">
              <tr>
                <td>
                  <table width="100%" border="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="#000022" class="text"><span style="font-size: 14;font-weight: bold;">Where have all the mobs gone?</span><a href="http://www.webwizguide.info"></a>&nbsp;</td>
                    </tr>
                    <tr> 
                      <td bgcolor="414f6e" class="text">
		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text"><P>Well...it's official folks. Planes of Power has passed the point of critical mass. Four raid forces are in the Elemental Planes, and maybe four more are at the point where they are spending more time working on flags than gearing up. Which means that decent raid mobs have become a rare spawn once again. A thought occurred to me while we were waiting to send <A href="http://eqbeastiary.allakhazam.com/search.shtml?id=11023" target=_blank>Krziik the Mighty</A> to a watery grave. </P>
<P>How cool would it be to introduce instancing (a la Lost Dungeons of Norrath) into the existing game? Feel like taking on Agnarr tonight? No problem - grab all your flagged members, head on over to the EQ Dungeon Master and away you go. Notice I said "flagged members". Here's the beauty of this system. For exp groups - you don't need the flags for any zones up to Plane of Tactics (current setup), but if you want to take down Agnarr, then by God, you'll do it with only the people who are flagged. Eliminate the whole non-flagged ratio system for raids. Since you can do the flag mob anytime you want, backflagging becomes less of a chore, and adds to the variety of the game. </P>
<P>Extend instancing to everything post-Kunark, and now the only thing standing in the way of a guild's advancement is the amount of time they are willing to expend to learn the encounters until they defeat them.&nbsp; I doubt Sony would ever go for something like this on the scale I have proposed - but think of how much bad blood this could eliminate...<BR></P>
<P>As I said before, Krziik the Mighty died a painful death last night. On the way there, Shilude picked up a nice new toy:</P>
