		    <table width="100%" border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2">
                     <tr>
                      <td align="left" class="text">Another very quiet night in VM-ville.  We spent the night in Torment farming pieces for another Saryn key.  The highlights of the evening were the officer promotions as well as guildinvites for two new members.<br>So without further ado...<br><br><b>New Members</b><br><ul><li>Millikin (Ranger)</li><li>Washou (Druid)</li></ul>Welcome to the guild, both of you.<br><br><b>Officer Promotions</b><br><ul><li>Galeni</li><li>Xelera</li><li>Genalen (Lead Tank)</li><li>Keawen (Recruit Officer)</li><li>Shaekee (Guild Scribe)</li><li>Eadric (Raid Leader)</li></ul>Congratulations to all the new officers.<br><br><b>Harry Potter Update</b><br>Tovarich is about 1/4 of the way through the book.  No, he doesn't know who dies yet.<br><br><b>In other news...</b><br><ul><li>Sally Ride, America's first woman in space, was inducted into the U.S. Astronaut Hall of Fame on Saturday, almost 20 years to the day that she rocketed into history</li><li>Chief Justice William H. Rehnquist, 78, and Justice Sandra Day O'Connor, 73, are the main objects of retirement speculation because of their ages and their presumed desire to allow a Republican president to pick a successor.</li><li>A federal district court dismissed a request by the one-time plaintiff known as "Jane Roe" to reconsider the landmark U.S. Supreme Court decision that legalized abortion 30 years ago</li><li>A city firefighter in Pontiac, MI has been accused of pointing a gun at his wife when she tried to stop him from watching Internet pornography.</li>&nbsp;</td>
